== KFold / RepeatedKFold / RepeatedStratifiedKFold shuffle semantics
ok   KFold(shuffle=True, random_state=7): indices shuffled once by RandomState(7).shuffle, then cut into consecutive folds (sizes 6,6,6,5)  (test sizes [6, 6, 6, 5])
ok   KFold(shuffle=True, random_state=int): identical splits on repeated split() calls
ok   KFold(shuffle=True, random_state=RandomState instance): each split() call draws a new shuffle (glossary: 'different across calls')
FAIL KFold(shuffle=False, random_state=0): docstring says random_state then 'has no effect'  (constructor raises ValueError)
ok   RepeatedKFold user-guide example (random_state=12883823): [2 3][0 1] / [0 1][2 3] / [0 2][1 3] / [1 3][0 2]  ([([2, 3], [0, 1]), ([0, 1], [2, 3]), ([0, 2], [1, 3]), ([1, 3], [0, 2])])
ok   RepeatedKFold(3, n_repeats=4, random_state=3): one RandomState(3) drives successive KFold shuffles; 12 splits
ok   RepeatedKFold: every repetition's test folds partition the samples, and repetitions differ
ok   RepeatedStratifiedKFold(3, 3): 9 splits, each repetition a partition with per-class fold counts differing by <= 1
ok   _RepeatedSplits: cvargs must not contain random_state/shuffle (ValueError)
