== cross_validate
ok   cross_validate(scoring=[r2, neg_mae]): keys test_r2 / test_neg_mean_absolute_error / train_* / fit_time / score_time / estimator
ok   cross_validate test_r2 = R^2 of a fresh OLS fit on each training fold (hand-written OLS)
ok   cross_validate return_train_score: train_r2 = R^2 on the training fold itself
ok   cross_validate test_neg_mean_absolute_error = -MAE on the test fold
ok   cross_validate return_estimator: the i-th estimator is the fit on the i-th training fold
ok   cross_validate fit_time / score_time: one non-negative float per split
ok   cross_validate(scoring=dict): keys test_<name>; make_scorer(max_error) value = max |error| per fold
ok   cross_validate(error_score=-99): folds whose fit fails get test AND train score -99, others are real, FitFailedWarning raised  ([-1.28781779e-02 -9.90000000e+01 -9.90000000e+01 -9.90000000e+01])
ok   cross_validate(error_score='raise') re-raises the fit error
ok   cross_validate default error_score=np.nan
ok   cross_validate(return_indices=True): indices['train'/'test'] are the splitter's folds
FAIL cross_validate(return_indices=True): docstring 'a list of integer-dtyped NumPy arrays'  (container type tuple)
