ok   learning_curve scores: fit on train[:n] (prefix of the fold's training indices), train score on that subset, test on the fold
ok   learning_curve: tiny fractions clipped to 1 sample and duplicates removed with a RuntimeWarning  ([np.int64(1), np.int64(41)])
ok   learning_curve integer train_sizes are absolute and returned sorted
ok   learning_curve integer train_size above n_max (first fold) raises ValueError
ok   learning_curve(exploit_incremental_learning=True): partial_fit on consecutive chunks 10, 15, 35 per fold  ([10, 15, 35])
ok   learning_curve incremental scores equal refitting on train[:n] (running mean = prefix mean)
ok   learning_curve(shuffle=True, random_state=11): each fold's training indices permuted by one RandomState(11) in fold order, prefixes taken
ok   learning_curve(return_times=True): 5 outputs, fit/score times of shape (n_ticks, n_folds)
ok   validation_curve(Ridge, alpha in [0.1, 10, 1000]): scores shape (3 params, 4 folds) = closed-form ridge per fold (test and train)
