== RandomizedSearchCV / multi-metric GridSearchCV / ranks
ok   RandomizedSearchCV(n_iter=7, random_state=8): 7 candidates = the replicated draws (distribution + list)
ok   RandomizedSearchCV with only lists and n_iter > grid: each of the 4 settings evaluated exactly once
ok   RandomizedSearchCV(refit=callable): best_index_ = the callable's return value, best_params_ = params[best_index_]
ok   refit=callable: 'the best_score_ attribute will not be available'
ok   rank_test_score: tied means share the MIN rank (most_frequent = prior -> 1, 1, then 3)  (means [0.5  0.5  0.55], ranks [np.int32(2), np.int32(2), np.int32(1)])
ok   error_score=nan: the failing candidate (strategy='constant' without constant) has mean nan and FitFailedWarning
ok   error_score=nan: failed candidates are ranked last ('tied with the worst performers'), best_index_ is a valid candidate  (ranks [np.int32(2), np.int32(3), np.int32(1)], best_index_ 2)
ok   multi-metric GridSearchCV: split<i>_test_acc / _nll and mean_test_* recomputed per fold
ok   multi-metric GridSearchCV(refit='nll'): best_index_ = argmax mean_test_nll, best_score_ = that mean (not accuracy)
ok   multi-metric with refit=False: no best_estimator_ / best_index_ exposed
ok   multi-metric with refit=True raises ValueError (must name a scorer or be callable)
